    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Kadane variant</span><span class=\"chip accent\">1-D DP</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-product-subarray/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 152</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Maximum Product Subarray</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Kadane for sums keeps one number, \"the best sum ending here\". For products one number is not enough: a negative value turns the most negative product into the largest one. Keep both the largest and the smallest product ending at each index, swap them on a negative, and the scan stays O(n) time, O(1) space.</p>\n"
  },
